<!--
  Cowrie honeypot, custom decoders
  =================================
  Cowrie writes events as one JSON object per line (cowrie.json). Wazuh's
  built-in JSON decoder parses these automatically when the log source is
  declared with <log_format>json</log_format> in ossec.conf, exposing every
  JSON key (eventid, src_ip, username, password, input, url, ...) as a
  dynamic field that rules can match on directly.

  Because the data is already structured JSON, NO regex field-extraction
  decoder is required, that is the correct engineering choice here, and the
  detection logic lives entirely in rules/local_rules.xml.

  This file is kept as the place to add decoders if we later ingest a
  non-JSON Cowrie text log (e.g. cowrie.log) or another honeypot.
-->
